course: dictionary
lesson: 12105
title: Cohort: a group that belongs together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A cohort is a group of people who have something in common, such as the same age or the same starting year. «This year's cohort started Reception in September.» The clues are "this year's" and "started", so a cohort is a whole group of children who began together.
explain: The word also appears in science and history. «The researchers followed a cohort of two thousand people for twenty years.» Here a cohort is a group studied together over time. «Each Roman legion was made up of ten cohorts.» Here a cohort is a unit of soldiers, about 480 men.
explain: Sometimes the word is informal. «Her cohort of fans waited outside the stadium.» Here a cohort is a supporter or companion. To check your meaning, swap in "group of people" and see if the sentence still makes sense. If it does, cohort fits.
fact: A cohort is a group of people who have something in common.
fact: In school, a cohort is often all the pupils who are in the same year group.
fact: In research, a cohort study follows the same group of people over time.
fact: In Roman history, a cohort was a unit of about 480 soldiers.
fact: Informally, a cohort can mean a supporter or companion of someone.
exercise: «The school's cohort of Year 5 pupils went on a trip.» What does cohort mean here? | A kind of school bag | A type of school dinner | A teacher's desk | *A group of pupils who started school together
exercise: In Roman history, a cohort was a unit of soldiers. About how many men were in one cohort? | *About 480 men | Just one man | About 5,000 men | About 50 men
exercise: «Scientists used a cohort study to follow children born in 2010.» What is a cohort study? | *A study that follows the same group of people over time | A study of old coins | A quick test with only one person | A study of the weather only
test: «She is a loyal cohort of the football club.» What does cohort mean in this sentence? | A kind of ball | *A supporter or companion | A distant star | A cold drink
test: Which word means a group of people who started school in the same year? | *cohort | cabbage | cavern | cushion
exam: The head teacher says, «Our cohort is the largest in the school's history.» What does cohort mean? | A type of weather | A lost property box | *A group of people with something in common | A single soldier
